  {
    "event_id": "e0003",
    "tool": "read_file",
    "arguments": {
      "path": "/docs/accounting.txt"
    },
    "response": {
      "path": "/docs/accounting.txt",
      "content": "All money is integer cents. No borrowing, refunds, resale, or terminal stock value.\nThe invoice debits the full item and shipping total immediately. Available stock stays zero until delivery.\nA round starts on day 2*stage and ends two days later. Both suppliers arrive by its market deadline.\nAt settle: record physical delivery, sell only the demanded product at the fixed public price, expire every unsold unit, then pay the operating fee. No stock carries into the next round.\nEach round requires units_per_case requests of one product; price cannot suppress this denominator.\nThe business service contract closes irreversibly on any missed request. It also closes if the maximum possible future cash cannot reach the published cash target.\nStatus/ledger expose past accounting only. Invalid operations leave all domain state unchanged.\nForecast rules: current = demand bit; xor_calibration = demand XOR calibration; xor_calibration_previous = demand XOR calibration XOR previous demand (previous=0 initially).\nA round offers one diagnostic sample, either forecast or assay. Calibration is separate and can be performed once in any open round. Sample/calibration must precede the irreversible order.\nThe candidate-world list is complete and does not mark the true row. In the transfer family both products occur somewhere, so previous outcomes can occasionally determine a later demand.\n",
      "event_id": "e0003",
      "cost_used": 3
    },
